   "text": "Arrange the sentences into a logical paragraph. Type the order (e.g. 12345).\n\n1. Yet even the camera's image must be cropped, scaled, labelled and layered before anyone can use it to find a road.\n2. Its makers decided what to include, what to omit, and which city to place at the centre, and every such choice declared what a culture valued.\n3. The argument has not vanished, then; it has merely moved from the drawing table to the interface.\n4. For most of history, a map was an argument about the world rather than a picture of it.\n5. Satellite imagery appeared to end this tradition of deliberate selection by replacing the mapmaker's choices with the indifferent eye of the camera.",
